ntime", "call_id": "toolu_015B3GJpB7G1rG83T45seArW", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 412523, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015B3GJpB7G1rG83T45seArW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 417631, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The test checks that 2.665 rounds to 2.66, which only happens with banker's rounding, so the nightly build failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **FIN-212:** I couldn't confirm the requirement against the advisory itself because the advisory lookup said FIN-212 doesn't exist. The fix is based on the test and the existing docstring, which both ask for banker's rounding.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0161Kyzf9eQy1sTS2nSZ7oyz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011o7vw6PvGK6HXcD647L9Ay", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ASw62ZwHDJweYnhaMM9qUK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01S1kupjjzapeixQxPhy2hMV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KM58mRktU7eHuMPUhsmREc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NP71Us9Vi2aTdc8YofFmjn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RNCQ5Fmce1r9UzcxgYfixk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015B3GJpB7G1rG83T45seArW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN)", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The test checks that 2.665 rounds to 2.66, which only happens with banker's rounding, so the nightly build failed.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **FIN-212:** I couldn't confirm the requirement against the advisory itself because the advisory lookup said FIN-212 doesn't exist. The fix is based on the test and the existing docstring, which both ask for banker's rounding.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}